# Game Architecture & Validation

## Layer boundaries (keep systems decoupled)

- `src/core/**` is the pure game logic. It MUST NOT import from `three`, touch
  the DOM/`window`/`document`, or import from `src/render`, `src/ui`, `src/fx`,
  or `src/app`. Keep it portable and unit-testable.
- The core communicates outward ONLY by emitting events on `EventBus`
  (`src/core/events/EventBus.ts`) and exposing a small command API on
  `GameCore`. Presentation layers subscribe; the core never knows who listens.
- `src/render` (Three.js), `src/ui` (DOM), and `src/fx` (juice) are pure
  subscribers/consumers. They may read snapshots and listen to events; they
  MUST NOT mutate game state directly.
- Polish (screenshake, squash, popups, flashes) lives in `src/fx` and must be
  toggleable (`Juice.enabled`). Disabling FX must never change game logic,
  numbers, or the HUD.
- All balance/tunables live in `src/core/config/**`. Do not hardcode balance
  numbers inside systems.

## Determinism

- All randomness goes through the seedable `Rng` (`src/core/rng/Rng.ts`). Never
  call `Math.random()` in `src/core`. This keeps tests reproducible and saves
  portable.

## Validation workflow (run after substantive changes)

1. `npm run typecheck` and `npm test` must pass. Add/extend headless tests in
   `tests/` for new core behavior, using a fixed seed and the debug commands.
2. For anything visual or interactive, verify in the browser:
   - start the dev server (`npm run dev`),
   - open it with the Cursor Browser tool using a fixed seed
     (e.g. `http://localhost:5173/?seed=42`),
   - drive the game via the `window.__GAME` debug API (see `src/app/debug.ts`),
   - take a screenshot to confirm the 9:16 layout and the change.
3. Prefer expanding the `window.__GAME` debug API over manual clicking so
   changes can be validated deterministically.
